      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (25%):</strong> N1 fails (p=0.90) and N3 materializes (p=0.28) — US strikes continue without ceasefire while Iran conducts a ballistic or cruise missile attack against GCC sovereign territory or a US military installation, drawing Gulf states directly into the conflict.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (65%):</strong> N1 fails (p=0.90) and N3 does not materialize (p=0.72) — US strikes continue, Hormuz remains at 8-11% of normal throughput, IRGC sustains Hormuz-denial posture without crossing to GCC ballistic escalation, and Pakistan's mediation finds no confirmed bilateral session.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (10%):</strong> N1 resolves YES (p=0.10) — a bilaterally confirmed ceasefire or formal pause is announced before July 20, with no observed diplomatic precursor currently supporting this path.</p>
